From 6aaceec695508dc22014761225414226ec23277d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:12:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 118/144] media: i2c: add initial Sony IMX615 RAW10 sensor
 driver

Implement the OnePlus 13 front sensor with its 19.2 MHz clock, ordered three-supply power sequence and 1640x1232 four-lane D-PHY mode. Expose exposure, analogue gain, vertical blanking and the solid-colour test pattern. Keep runtime power and failed-stream cleanup bounded. Register values are derived from the dodgefront sensor module identified in the table header.

Import-Patch: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm8750/dodge/patches/7.3/0150-media-i2c-add-initial-Sony-IMX615-RAW10-sensor-drive.patch
Import-SHA256: 6b079fd51460f832cec251f8fc06d57e4030810abd38d8f1d1a35318467627fe
Import-Provenance: mail headers
(cherry picked from commit 03e4a2e6f4df5809b06740e59b7c6a3579e41ad9)
---
 drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig       |  10 +
 drivers/media/i2c/Makefile      |   2 +
 drivers/media/i2c/imx615-regs.h | 328 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/media/i2c/imx615.c      | 458 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 798 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/media/i2c/imx615-regs.h
